# apps/account environment template. Copy to .env.local for local dev,
# or set these via your CI's secret store for production builds.
# .env.local is gitignored; only .env.example is committed.
#
# Pimlico ERC-4337 bundler + paymaster.
# Get a key at https://dashboard.pimlico.io (see docs/self-host-wallet.md
# for the dashboard walkthrough — origin restriction + sponsorship policy
# are mandatory for safe production use).
#
# Vite inlines VITE_-prefixed env into the bundle at build time. That
# means the API key ends up in the published JS, which is FINE because
# the Pimlico dashboard restricts it to:
#   1. Allowed Origins:  https://id.kon.xyz (+ http://localhost:5175 for dev)
#   2. Allowed Chains:   8453 (Base mainnet), 84532 (Base Sepolia)
#   3. Sponsorship Policy: only sponsors KON's ENS Registry +
#      Public Resolver calls, with strict function-selector + gas caps
# An attacker who extracts the key from the bundle cannot use it for
# anything outside this allowlist.
VITE_PIMLICO_API_KEY=

# Sponsorship policy id from the Pimlico dashboard. Empty = no paymaster
# (user's Safe pays gas itself, which is fine for testing but a poor UX
# for real organizers). Set this once you've created the policy under
# "Sponsorship Policies" in the dashboard.
VITE_PIMLICO_SPONSORSHIP_POLICY_ID=
